        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f1f2e8b2-82f5-5913-9b10-56c77cdc472b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Dubai Textile Souk, Dubai Gold Souk, Dubai Spice Souk, Dubai Creek, Bur Dubai, Deira, Dubai, United Arab Emirates\n- Organizations: Iranian Mosque, Ali ibn Abi Talib Iranian Mosque\n- Topics: textile markets, jewellery trade, abra boats, Shia mosques\n\nFacts:\n- The Dubai Textile Souk, also known as the Old Textile Souk, is a traditional textile market in the historic Bur Dubai neighbourhood of Dubai.\n- The Dubai Spice Souk and Dubai Gold Souk are located across Dubai Creek in Deira, opposite the Dubai Textile Souk.\n- Special abra boats provide access across Dubai Creek between the Dubai Textile Souk area and the souks in Deira.\n- The Dubai Gold Souk consists of over 300 retailers, most of whom are jewellery traders.\n- The Iranian Mosque, also known as the Ali ibn Abi Talib Iranian Mosque, is a Shia mosque near the old Dubai Textile Souk in Bur Dubai, Dubai, United Arab Emirates.",
